    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "About 60 million years ago, Mount Qomolangma began to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "form",
            "ref": "v-form"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". That was a long time ago. But for mountains, it’s young. The name “Qomolangma” is from "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Tibetan",
            "zh": "藏语"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". It means “Mother Goddess of the Earth”"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "大地之母"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Mount Qomolangma is 8848.86 metres high. It’s the world’s highest mountain. Many people have tried to climb to the top. The best weather for "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "reaching",
            "ref": "v-reach"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the top arrives in May. The winds are usually "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "gentler",
            "ref": "v-gentle"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". It’s not too cold, either."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "So, what’s the summit"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "山顶"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " like? It’s a small dome"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "圆顶状物"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of snow. It’s about the size of a dining room table. There’s room for about six climbers to stand at one time. The "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "view",
            "ref": "v-view"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " is great from there."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "On busy days, climbers must "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "take turns",
            "ref": "v-take-turns"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to truly stand on top of the world! But in the past, it was very hard to reach the top. How hard? Watch the film "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "The Climbers"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "《攀登者》"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
